gned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{{(\\,5\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}= \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -25\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -21\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186409818 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$"] [:db/cas 17592186409818 :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-14 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=8.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(8)=-14\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-6)+8=2.$" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -16\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-14 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=8.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(8)=-14\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-6)+8=2.$"] [:db/cas 17592186409819 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x