\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x(t)$\n- **III.** ${x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}x(t)$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186413697 :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186413698 :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186413699 :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] [:db/cas 17592186413700 :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186413701 :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186413702 :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] [:db/cas 17592186413703 :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] [:db/cas 17592186413704 :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186413705 :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] [:db/cas 17592186413706 :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] [:db/cas 17592186413707 :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] [:db/cas 17592186413708 :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] [:db/cas 17592186413709 :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] [:db/cas 17592186413710 :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] [:db/cas 17592186413711 :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] [:db/cas 17592186413715 :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ that correspond to eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ respectively. What is the general solution of the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)?$" "Let ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ that correspond to eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ respectively. What is the general solution of the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)?$"] [:db/cas 17592186413715 :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$" "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186413716 :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186413737 :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨1,-2,1⟩,\\,p=⟨3,-1,2⟩,$ and $q=⟨4,2,0⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,2⟩-⟨1,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨4,2,0⟩-⟨1,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,4,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow,  we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-5i+5j+5k \\\\  & =⟨-5,5,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =⟨3,-1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =-10 \\\\ -5x+5y+5z & =-10 \\\\ -5x+5y+5z+10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨1,-2,1⟩,\\,p=⟨3,-1,2⟩,$ and $q=⟨4,2,0⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,2⟩-⟨1,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨4,2,0⟩-⟨1,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,4,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow,  we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-5i+5j+5k \\\\  & =⟨-5,5,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =⟨3,-1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =-10 \\\\ -5x+5y+5z & =-10 \\\\ -5x+5y+5z+10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186413748 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10{e}^{9}-4{e}^{-6} \\\\ -10{e}^{9}+2{e}^{-6}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}10{e}^{9}-4{e}^{-6} \\\\ -10{e}^{9}+2{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186413749 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}"] [:db/cas 17592186413750 :answer/value "x(t)=2{e}^{-3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+2[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" "x(t)=2{e}^{-3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+2\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}"] [:db/cas 17592186413751 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}"] [:db/cas 17592186413752 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10{e}^{9}+12{e}^{-6} \\\\ 10{e}^{9}-6{e}^{-6}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-10{e}^{9}+12{e}^{-6} \\\\ 10{e}^{9}-6{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186413758 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}"] [:db/cas 17592186413759 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{9}+{e}^{-6} \\\\ -{e}^{9}-{e}^{-6}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{9}+{e}^{-6} \\\\ -{e}^{9}-{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186413760 :answer/value "x(t)={e}^{-3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+2e[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" "x(t)={e}^{-3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+2e\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}"] [:db/cas 17592186413761 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}512{e}^{-6} \\\\ 5{e}^{9}-2{e}^{-6}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}512{e}^{-6} \\\\ 5{e}^{9}-2{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186413763 :answer/value "x(t)={e}^{-2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+2[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" "x(t)={e}^{-2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+2\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}"] [:db/cas 17592186413766 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}"] [:db/cas 17592186413767 :answer/value "x(t)={e}^{-3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-5t}+2e[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" "x(t)={e}^{-3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-5t}+2e\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}"] [:db/cas 17592186413768 :answer/value "x(t)={e}^{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-5t}+2e[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" "x(t)={e}^{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-5t}+2e\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}"] [:db/cas 17592186413769 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10{e}^{9} \\\\ 5{e}^{9}+6{e}^{-6}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-10{e}^{9} \\\\ 5{e}^{9}+6{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186413771 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}"] [:db/cas 17592186413787 :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186413787 :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {