gned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=5 \\\\ 0x+0y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=6$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=6,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 21\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 21\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 21\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=5 \\\\ 0x+0y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=6$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=6,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."] [:db/cas 17592186414184 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form."] [:db/cas 17592186414184 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 